IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er4-nouns`
IMPORT `er4-part3-1-weeks`

-- Tests of regs 76.19, 76.2 and 76.21 (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1247-1271). Every expected value is written by hand from the
-- text. The Act's own figures that the formulas read (35 and 61 of s 12(3)(b), 40 of s 12(4)(b)(i), 15 and 50 of s 12)
-- are fed in as inputs, as in the module; the tests do not assert them as law.

§ `Reg 76.19(1) -- provincial weeks count against the maximum`

#ASSERT `reg 76.19(1) the provincial benefits paid for the week are considered to be benefits paid in respect of a week under the Act` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.19(1) the provincial benefits paid for the week are considered to be benefits paid in respect of a week under the Act` FALSE
-- 20 weeks under the Act and 10 weeks of provincial benefits: 30 weeks counted.
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(1)(a) the weeks counted toward the overall maximum number of weeks under paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act taken together` 20 10 EQUALS 30
-- Against an overall maximum of 50: 20 weeks left; exactly 50 counted leaves none; 51 counted is not answered by the text.
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(1)(a) the weeks left within the overall maximum` 50 20 10 EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(1)(a) the weeks left within the overall maximum` 50 40 10 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(1)(a) the weeks left within the overall maximum` 50 40 11 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(1)(b) the weeks counted toward the maximum number of weeks under subsection 12(4) of the Act` 15 20 EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(1)(b) the weeks left within the maximum under subsection 12(4)` 40 15 20 EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(1)(b) the weeks left within the maximum under subsection 12(4)` 40 15 26 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 76.19(1.1) -- the benefit period`

#ASSERT `reg 76.19(1.1) a benefit period is deemed to be established` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.19(1.1) a benefit period is deemed to be established` FALSE
-- Deemed to have begun the same week only if the claimant would have been entitled to the corresponding types of benefits.
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(1.1) the week in which the benefit period is deemed to have begun` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(1.1) the week in which the benefit period is deemed to have begun` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(1.1) the week in which the benefit period is deemed to have begun` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 76.19(2) and (3) -- benefits paid at an accelerated rate`

-- The plan pays a type of benefit over 25 weeks at the accelerated rate where 35 weeks is the non-accelerated maximum:
-- 10 weeks paid represent 10 x 35/25 = 14 weeks under the Act.
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(2) the number of weeks of benefits that the weeks of provincial benefits represent under the Act, before rounding` 10 35 25 EQUALS JUST 14
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(2) the number of weeks of benefits that the weeks of provincial benefits represent under the Act, before rounding` 10 35 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Rounding: to the nearest week, the higher when equidistant.
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(3) the number of weeks rounded to the nearest multiple of one week, the higher multiple when equidistant` 7 EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(3) the number of weeks rounded to the nearest multiple of one week, the higher multiple when equidistant` 7.49 EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(3) the number of weeks rounded to the nearest multiple of one week, the higher multiple when equidistant` 7.5 EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(3) the number of weeks rounded to the nearest multiple of one week, the higher multiple when equidistant` 7.51 EQUALS 8
-- Both together, with a ratio of 15/10 = 1.5: 3 weeks give 4.5, rounded up to 5; 5 weeks give 7.5, rounded up to 8; 4 weeks give 6.
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(2) and (3) the weeks of provincial benefits as weeks under the Act` TRUE 3 15 10 EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(2) and (3) the weeks of provincial benefits as weeks under the Act` TRUE 5 15 10 EQUALS JUST 8
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(2) and (3) the weeks of provincial benefits as weeks under the Act` TRUE 4 15 10 EQUALS JUST 6
-- 10 x 35/25 = 14 exactly; and 12 x 35/25 = 16.8 rounds to 17.
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(2) and (3) the weeks of provincial benefits as weeks under the Act` TRUE 10 35 25 EQUALS JUST 14
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(2) and (3) the weeks of provincial benefits as weeks under the Act` TRUE 12 35 25 EQUALS JUST 17
-- Not paid at the accelerated rate: each week is a week.
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(2) and (3) the weeks of provincial benefits as weeks under the Act` FALSE 7 35 25 EQUALS JUST 7
#ASSERT `reg 76.19(2) and (3) the weeks of provincial benefits as weeks under the Act` TRUE 7 35 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 76.2 -- excess weeks of provincial benefits are not taken into account`

-- The Act allows 35 weeks and the plan up to 40: the 5 excess weeks do not count.
#ASSERT `reg 76.2 the weeks of provincial benefits that are taken into account in determining the maximum number of weeks` 35 40 38 EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `reg 76.2 the weeks of provincial benefits that are taken into account in determining the maximum number of weeks` 35 40 30 EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `reg 76.2 the weeks of provincial benefits that are taken into account in determining the maximum number of weeks` 35 40 40 EQUALS 35
-- The plan allows no more than the Act: every week counts.
#ASSERT `reg 76.2 the weeks of provincial benefits that are taken into account in determining the maximum number of weeks` 40 40 38 EQUALS 38
#ASSERT `reg 76.2 the weeks of provincial benefits that are taken into account in determining the maximum number of weeks` 40 35 30 EQUALS 30
-- The plan allows 18 weeks, the Act 15: 17 weeks paid, 15 count.
#ASSERT `reg 76.2 the weeks of provincial benefits that are taken into account in determining the maximum number of weeks` 15 18 17 EQUALS 15

§ `Reg 76.21(1) -- two persons caring for the same child`

#ASSERT `reg 76.21(1) subsection (2) applies in respect of the two persons` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.21(1) subsection (2) applies in respect of the two persons` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.21(1) subsection (2) applies in respect of the two persons` FALSE TRUE

§ `Reg 76.21(2) -- the claimant's share`

-- An odd number of weeks, 35: the claimant who applied first gets 1 + (35-1)/2 = 18; the other way round, (35-1)/2 = 17.
#ASSERT `reg 76.21(2) the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant, subject to subsection (3)` 35 `er4 the person claiming benefits under the Act made the earlier application` FALSE EQUALS JUST 18
#ASSERT `reg 76.21(2) the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant, subject to subsection (3)` 35 `er4 the provincial applicant made the earlier application` FALSE EQUALS JUST 17
-- An even number, 36: half whoever applied first.
#ASSERT `reg 76.21(2) the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant, subject to subsection (3)` 36 `er4 the person claiming benefits under the Act made the earlier application` FALSE EQUALS JUST 18
#ASSERT `reg 76.21(2) the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant, subject to subsection (3)` 36 `er4 the provincial applicant made the earlier application` FALSE EQUALS JUST 18
-- Small numbers.
#ASSERT `reg 76.21(2) the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant, subject to subsection (3)` 1 `er4 the person claiming benefits under the Act made the earlier application` FALSE EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `reg 76.21(2) the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant, subject to subsection (3)` 1 `er4 the provincial applicant made the earlier application` FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `reg 76.21(2) the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant, subject to subsection (3)` 0 `er4 the provincial applicant made the earlier application` FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
-- An agreement or a court order: the subsection gives no number.
#ASSERT `reg 76.21(2) the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant, subject to subsection (3)` 35 `er4 the provincial applicant made the earlier application` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 76.21(3) and (4) -- the most weeks that may be paid`

-- A = 40 (s 12(4)(b)(i) divided), C = 61, D = 35, as the Act states them; B = 15 weeks paid to the provincial applicant.
#ASSERT `reg 76.21(3)(a) the most weeks payable to a claimant who elected the 35-week maximum` 40 15 EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `reg 76.21(3)(a) the most weeks payable to a claimant who elected the 35-week maximum` 40 0 EQUALS 40
-- (40 - 15) x 61 / 35 = 43.57..., rounded down to 43; (40 - 0) x 61 / 35 = 69.71..., rounded down to 69.
#ASSERT `reg 76.21(3)(b) the most weeks payable to a claimant who elected the 61-week maximum` 40 15 61 35 EQUALS JUST 43
#ASSERT `reg 76.21(3)(b) the most weeks payable to a claimant who elected the 61-week maximum` 40 0 61 35 EQUALS JUST 69
-- An exact result is not rounded: (35 - 0) x 61 / 35 = 61.
#ASSERT `reg 76.21(3)(b) the most weeks payable to a claimant who elected the 61-week maximum` 35 0 61 35 EQUALS JUST 61
#ASSERT `reg 76.21(3)(b) the most weeks payable to a claimant who elected the 61-week maximum` 40 15 61 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 76.21(3) the most weeks that may be paid to the claimant` `the 35-week maximum` 40 15 61 35 EQUALS JUST 25
#ASSERT `reg 76.21(3) the most weeks that may be paid to the claimant` `the 61-week maximum` 40 15 61 35 EQUALS JUST 43
-- (4): the maximum is 35 or 61 according to the election.
#ASSERT `reg 76.21(4) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid to the claimant in accordance with the election` `the 35-week maximum` 35 61 EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `reg 76.21(4) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid to the claimant in accordance with the election` `the 61-week maximum` 35 61 EQUALS 61

§ `Reg 76.21 -- the weeks payable to the claimant`

-- Arguments: weeks otherwise entitled, who applied first, agreement or order, election, A, B, C, D.
-- 35 weeks, claimant applied first: share 18; cap 40 - 15 = 25; ceiling 35: 18.
#ASSERT `reg 76.21 the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant` 35 `er4 the person claiming benefits under the Act made the earlier application` FALSE `the 35-week maximum` 40 15 61 35 EQUALS JUST 18
-- The cap binds: provincial applicant was paid 30 weeks, cap 40 - 30 = 10, below the share of 18.
#ASSERT `reg 76.21 the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant` 35 `er4 the person claiming benefits under the Act made the earlier application` FALSE `the 35-week maximum` 40 30 61 35 EQUALS JUST 10
-- 61 weeks, provincial applicant first: share 30; cap 69 (B = 0); ceiling 61: 30.
#ASSERT `reg 76.21 the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant` 61 `er4 the provincial applicant made the earlier application` FALSE `the 61-week maximum` 40 0 61 35 EQUALS JUST 30
-- 61-week election with B = 30: cap floor(10 x 61/35) = 17, below the share of 30.
#ASSERT `reg 76.21 the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant` 61 `er4 the provincial applicant made the earlier application` FALSE `the 61-week maximum` 40 30 61 35 EQUALS JUST 17
-- An agreement: the regulation gives no number.
#ASSERT `reg 76.21 the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant` 35 `er4 the provincial applicant made the earlier application` TRUE `the 35-week maximum` 40 15 61 35 EQUALS NOTHING
